<title>SRI LANKA: Kelani Valley up on growth prospects.</title>
<headline>Kelani Valley up on growth prospects.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kelani Valley Plantations Ltd rose 4.84 percent or 1.50 rupees to 32.50, in early Monday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Buyers are going for all tea firms because profits in the sector are seen having another good year in 1997,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Plantations, led by tea, are seen having another good year due to continued demand from the commonwealth of independent states and Middle East. The years of 1995 and 1996 were good years due to demand from these two markets.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
